  "notes": "Waiver filing, cash basis, Exhibit A all-funds statement. The filing contains two versions of each page; the versions with a red X (trimmed pp2, 4, 6) are void and were not used; unmarked pp1, 3, 5 used. The crossed-out version differs (General receipts 205,038.22 total, no transfers, different disbursement totals); not recorded as a discrepancy beyond this note. Governmental = General, Street, Cemetery, Bond; business-type = Water, Sewer. Transfers: Bond to Cemetery 47,422.84, Bond to General 57,548.73, Sewer to Water 124,324.60 (p5 schedule; total 229,296.17 ties to line 20). General fund transfer-in cell on p1 reads 57,548.73 at 200 dpi, consistent with column total 262,586.95 and the p5 schedule. Property tax Bond cell has a handwritten overlay; amount derived. Beginning/ending cash are subtotals of net cash + investments so roll-forward ties: 863,443.26 + 312,893.88 - 388,375.63 + 104,971.57 - 104,971.57 = 787,961.51; business 281,904.05 + 178,888.64 - 84,659.61 = 376,133.08. Receipts items exclude transfers; business receipts and disbursements exclude the sewer-to-water transfer. No separate balance sheet, so the ending balance page is used. Attempt 2 (charges-for-services re-check): Water and Sewer 'Local Receipts: Other' recategorised from charges for services/fees to Utility Charges (each is its utility fund's only operating receipt; no breakdown printed, kept under review). Governmental 'Local Receipts: Other' lines stay other (nothing in the filing explains them). Read pages 1-6 of 6"
